      "title": "How it works",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "1. Set folder_path to a folder of images. With auto_run_folder on, one Run walks the whole folder; turn it off to caption one image per run using index.\n2. Load Qwen3.5 and Generate Text write a caption for each image. Edit the prompt to change the style, for example tags instead of sentences.\n3. Save Caption writes a .txt next to each image with the same name, ready for LoRA training. overwrite is on by default, so turn it off to keep existing captions.\n4. Run Timer times the whole run and keeps a history."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "1. Set folder_path to a folder of images. With auto_run_folder on, one Run walks the whole folder; turn it off to caption one image per run using index.\n2. Load Qwen3.5 and Generate Text write a caption for each image. Edit the prompt to change the style, for example tags instead of sentences.\n3. Save Caption writes a .txt next to each image with the same name, ready for LoRA training. overwrite is on by default, so turn it off to keep existing captions.\n4. Run Timer times the whole run and keeps a history."
      },
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
